  "description": "What: the FLAME HELICOPTER (TKB 412 \u2014 the AH-64 airframe with a chin flame projector and its Hydra-70 pod; CE-3490 BA-9, docs/designs/air-attack/DESIGN_Breath_Attack.md \u00a77). On basic-desert 'Flame Helicopter', 60 m up at (100, 300), is ordered AirPlatformAttack on 'Squad Man 1' of a row of four hostile riflemen at x 400, y 288\u2026312; 'Armour Hunter', the same type 60 m up at (-1200, 560), on a hostile 'T-72' at (400, 560). Judge: the Flame Helicopter strafes low and breathes, two squad men burn and Squad Man 1 dies, and it climbs back above 50 m; the Armour Hunter never breathes on the tank (an armoured hull does not burn) and fires its rockets at it instead."
 },
